STYLE: A grand hand-made toy theatre production built from printed card. Every piece is a flat cutout of thick card about 4 mm thick, cut by hand with a craft knife. The front of each piece is painted like a page from a Korean painter's field sketchbook of 1950: soft charcoal line and grey ink wash with thin, rain-washed watercolour on warm hanji mulberry paper, with the long fibres of the paper visible, loose expressive brush and charcoal strokes, quiet tender faces drawn with a few lines. The colour is muted and wet: slate grey, mist white, earth brown, faded indigo, pine green, with one dull persimmon red for a few accents. Bold, simple shapes that read from the back row. Puppet joints are brass split pins. Palette: hanji paper #EDE6D6, charcoal #2B2A28, slate #5E6670, mist #C9CDD0, earth #6E5A44, indigo #3B4A66, pine #4E5E48, persimmon #B4553A, with raw card brown #A57E52 at cut edges. The mood is grief, tenderness and rain. Korea, June 1950.
CONSTRAINTS: No text, no characters, no letters, no numbers, no Hangul, no signs with writing, no logos, no signature, no watermark. No flags, no insignia, no armbands, no badges, no stars on caps, nothing that marks a side in the war. No real persons. No photographic people, no 3D render look, no plastic, no glossy finish, no anime style.
REFERENCES: Image 1 is the look reference. Match its charcoal, ink wash, hanji paper, palette and figure style. Do not copy its composition. Do not paint a theatre, a stage or curtains.
COMPOSITION: A tall portrait poster for this production, painted in the same charcoal and ink wash style as Image 1, like a hand-printed poster from a grand old playhouse. One calm, strong composition with a single clear focal point. A slim ornamental painted border frames the picture. Keep a plain, quiet band of warm cream paper across the top fifth of the poster and across the bottom sixth: lettering goes there later, so nothing is painted in those bands. No text anywhere.
SUBJECT: A young Korean man in soaked white cotton clothes stands at the head of a wooden rope bridge over a swollen river in the monsoon rain, his hand on the rope, watching his friend in a dark jacket cross away into the grey fog among refugees with bundles.
